# A run of comments read from its last one up (the skeptic seat's `s8`): a
# comment at column 0 above the `if` block's last comment was printed at the
# body's column, and pulled the block's last comment out with it, at exit 0.
# No comment of a run belongs to a shallower block than one after it, since
# printed in order a later one cannot sit deeper: both stay in the block.

function f(c: bool)
    if c
        print(1)
#        print(2)
        # the if block's last word
    print(3)

function main()
    f(c: true)
